hey guys we're at the end of 2020 can  you believe that  it's been one crazy unpredictable year  it's not been easy for most of us but as  we looked back at this year  what have some of your highlights been  let me know  in the comments below it's another new  year that also means  time to list down your new year's  resolution how many of you have set  fitness resolutions in the past have you  achieved it  or have you just forgotten about it  according to a study  sixty percent of people give up on their  resolution by february  by march a whopping eighty percent have  totally let it go i don't want you to be  one of the statistics  i want you to be part of that 20 who  succeed  and i know you can do it i'm going to  share with you  seven ways to succeed in your fitness  resolution  before you can embark on a successful  fitness journey you need to find  your why the inner motivation within you  take a moment to assess why do you so  desperately want to lose the weight  if your answer is because i'm overweight  that's not good enough  you need to dig deeper for instance it  might be for your wedding that is coming  up  or a health issue or perhaps your weight  might be preventing you from doing  certain things such as  spending more time playing with your  kids be honest and ask yourself  what is your why that will give you the  strength to carry you  through your fitness journey if your  reason for losing weight and looking fit  is merely aesthetic or to look like a  certain celebrity  or influencer i would suggest that you  re-evaluate your motivation  because this could lead to an unhealthy  obsession  both physically and emotionally it's  important to  love and accept yourself before you can  make any changes  we're all different perfect in our own  ways  and we should embrace that once you have  found your inner motivation  write it down because this will be your  key  to success  what does toning up or losing weight  actually mean to you  how would you measure it what would you  do how long will it take you to get  there  in order to succeed you need to set  smart goals  your goals need to be specific  measurable  attainable realistic and time-bound  but how many of us actually apply it so  grab a pen and paper and write down your  smart  goal it has been proven that people who  write down their goals  are more likely to achieve them by over  70 percent  you can either write it down in your  journal or if you're mostly on your  mobile  you can also type it into your phone and  make it your wallpaper  don't stress out about it there is no  right or wrong and sometimes  you wouldn't know what you want until  you start  writing things down specific instead of  just saying i want to lose weight and  tone up  dive deeper my goal is to lose 25 kilos  this year measurable that's a great  start now  let's measure and calculate how long it  will take you to achieve  your goal if you were to lose 25 kilos  in 12 months  that's an average of 2 kilos a month and  half a kilo a week  by adding quantity to your goals and  breaking it down to smaller goals  this will allow you to track and ensure  success rather than focusing on a big  number 25 kilos which can be  overwhelming and scary  you're focusing on half a kilo a week  which is more manageable and attainable  is it attainable yes the safe and  recommended weight loss  is between half to one kilo per week  the heavier you are the quicker you will  lose the weight  especially in the early stages because  you have more fat to burn  the lighter you are the longer it will  take because your body has  less fat to burn set a realistic goal so  that you know you can work towards it  and you're setting yourself up for  success i've received  lots of comments asking how can i lose  10 kilos in a couple of weeks or  how can i get a flat belly in two weeks  don't expect that to happen  you didn't put on all the weight over a  few weeks  hence it will take time to lose the  weight  be realistic with yourself if you're  ready to invest your time and effort and  stop looking for shortcuts  then do this with me time-bound every  goal needs to be  time-bound otherwise there is no urgency  to want to achieve it  in this case the time you have set for  yourself is 12 months  setting a smart goal is only one small  part of the puzzle  it means nothing if you don't have an  action plan how are you going to achieve  your goal  what steps do you need to take what do  you have to sacrifice  i like to call this the action and give  list  in order to get what you want you must  be willing to make changes  compromise get out of your comfort zone  do things you have never done before  and even make sacrifices what i want you  to do is to create  two columns the first column is action  what do i have to do in order to achieve  my goal  the second column is give what do i have  to give up so the action column can be  i'll hit the gym three times weekly i'll  cook  two healthy meals a day i'll hit 10 000  steps  daily i'll get at least seven to eight  hours of sleep  daily the gift column can be i'll eat  takeaways only twice a week i have to  wake up an hour earlier  to get my workout done i'll cut down on  alcohol and only go out for a drink once  a week  i will spend the weekend to prep my  meals for the week  it doesn't have to be a long list but  rather a short list that you can focus  on and turn them into positive habits  once you have written down the action  and gift list weigh out the balance of  each column  make sure it's realistic to your  schedule and lifestyle  and consciously tell yourself that  you're ready to commit  to these lifestyle changes  [Music]  if you're someone who hasn't been  physically active and has been eating  fast food and takeaways for many years  start small and slowly build up the  momentum no  i'm not expecting you to hit the gym  every single day or cook  every single meal if you try to change  too much  too quickly you're setting yourself up  for failure  take it step by step and develop a solid  foundation of fitness  and then build upon that foundation as  your fitness improves  if you have no idea where to start or  how to structure your own workout  program  then do check out my own fitness app  called feel i've created few with the  focus on three main pillars of wellness  which is exercise food and mindset  we offer new monthly guided workout  programs with a combination of strength  training and cardio  each workout is only 30 minutes long and  you get to do it at home plus  all the workouts are taught by  internationally certified trainers  so you know you're in safe hands we also  have  over 100 really simple recipes to get  you started  as well as short videos to help you  train your mindset  in order to succeed so do check it out  on fieldlife.com or  download on the app store and google  play we know fitness resolutions are  hard to keep  and to be honest motivation can quickly  disappear  hence by using fuel you will be able to  schedule your workout  build your momentum and keep you  accountable which  leads on to my next point  i truly believe that when you're able to  share your goals and progress with  like-minded people  it will give you a sense of  accountability they will also be able to  offer you support  and motivation when things get tough it  can either be a workout partner  a family member who cheers you on a  personal trainer or  even an online community where you can  share your journey with  such as on field app or even my youtube  channel  right here you are always welcome to  share your weight loss journey  ask questions and even support each  other that's what we are here for  but know this who you share your goals  with is extremely important  i would encourage you to just openly  share it with anyone and  everyone you know over sharing might not  be a positive thing  because these people may end up  sabotaging you  oh she's trying to lose weight oh come  on  one slice of cake will not make you fat  so  how much have you lost the harsh truth  is that  not everybody is going to be excited  about your goals  there will always be people who will try  to bring you down  and you don't need that energy in your  life this is  your life your body your goal  if they are not offering any support  instead they make you feel unworthy  and like a failure your best bet is to  stay away from them  you don't need to waste your time trying  to explain or share yourself  you don't owe them an explanation  neither should you feel guilty  if you choose to avoid them only share  with someone who truly cares and wants  the best for you  together you can keep each other updated  get tips  advice and encourage one another the  only way to know if you're on the right  path towards your goal  is to track your progress there are many  different ways  to track your progress that can be  keeping a workout journal  having a workout journal helps you  determine how much exercise you're  currently getting in  and allows you to see your progress  whether it's the number of steps you  take  the number of times you work out the  kilometers you jog  or the time spent in the gym it's also  an effective method  to track the exercises and amount of  weight you lifted in your previous  workouts  this way you'll know if you're getting  stronger remember that progress is not  just about  the number on the skill but it's also  about you  getting stronger physically and mentally  weigh yourself it's important to weigh  yourself to know if you're on track  with the amount you need to lose saying  that however  i don't want you to be obsessed over  weighing yourself  every single day and determine your  success solely based on the number on  the scale  only weigh yourself once a week and know  that your progress  is not solely determined by the number  on the scale  if you're wondering why the number on  the scale isn't moving  but you feel that your clothes fit  better and that you look  slimmer that's because you have  increased in muscle mass  and reduced in body fat this leads on to  the next point  check your body composition meaning the  percentage of  body fat versus muscle mass as you  strength train  you will build muscle and burn fat your  body fat percentage will go  down and your muscle mass will increase  but your weight remains  the same that's because one pound of  muscle is more  dense compared to one pound of fat so  even if your weight remains the same  you will look more firm and toned most  fitness and health clubs will have the  machine for you to check  your body composition next take a  picture  i love to take post workout selfies it's  not about being vain  but rather it's a great reminder to  myself that i've completed another  workout session  and that feels good when we see  ourselves every single day we don't  always notice  the changes but as you look back at all  the pictures  and compare photos from 6 to 12 weeks  apart  you will definitely see the differences  at the end of the day  when you review your progress you can  look at ways to improve  and also celebrate small successes along  the way  and the final step is to know that this  is not just another  new year's resolution it's a permanent  lifestyle change  it's not something you stop once you  have lost x amount of weight but rather  it's about setting you on a path to a  healthier and happier life  forever so you got to work towards  achieving what you want  every single day forget about going on  the fast lane  and because it's a journey there will be  lots of  ups and downs and i can tell you right  now it won't be a smooth journey and it  won't be easy  you'll have days when you feel extremely  motivated and out of the sudden  you might fall back into your old habit  of binge eating again  if you can foresee this you can better  prepare yourself when it's about to  happen  and overcome it with certain strategies  remember do not turn  relapses or temporary failures into  meltdowns  or excuses for giving up instead  acknowledge the mistakes look at ways on  how you can better manage it when it  happens  and recommit to the path i believe  that achieving our goals isn't about  willpower it's about developing the  right skills and strategies  and with the right execution it will  lead to success  let me know what's your fitness goal in  the comments below and how you plan on  achieving that  this is your space so i would encourage  you to leave your comments  regularly and keep me updated in your  progress do also check out my  description box as i've added a lot more  links  to guide you through your fitness  journey if you find this video to be  helpful  do share it on with someone who could  benefit from this hit  the like button subscribe to my youtube  channel for a lot more workout videos  recipes as well as fitness tips and  let's start  2021 strong
 

